        "tweets": [
            {
                "text": "I've found the most optically annoying and the least serdes/dsp demanding optical networking architecture: optical serializer with a mode-locked laser (OTDM) so that you can have wide and slow signals coming in, and dual-comb-like homodyne detection with the same comb source as LO and same set of delays so that the detector and TIA bandwidths can also be small. You just need to hold path length drift/pulse overlap to be sub 10s of fs, and the optical phase, the branch skew, pulse shape..",
