            },
            {
                "text": "- Qin2020: [5 nm Nanogap Electrodes and Arrays by Super-resolution Laser Lithography]( https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.nanolett.0c00978) Ti gap is made by converting to TiO2 and etch with HF+H2O2. Does not even require crazy fs lasers, it is just a few us laser pulse at 405 nm with 10-100 mW power. Claimed to be 10x faster than FIB. Could probably make it even faster with smarter optics.",
